_s <- \# _xWILD @@ # a real comment
_xWILD [min=1 match=(\#)]	### (1)

----------------------------------------------------

[
	["node", "_s"],
	["arrow", "<-"],
	["char", "\\#"],
	["constant", "_xWILD"],
	["region", "@@"],
	["comment", "# a real comment"],

	["constant", "_xWILD"],
	["modifiers", [
		["punctuation", "["],
		["attr-name", "min"],
		["operator", "="],
		["number", "1"],
		["attr-name", "match"],
		["operator", "="],
		["value-list", [
			["punctuation", "("],
			["char", "\\#"],
			["punctuation", ")"]
		]],
		["punctuation", "]"]
	]],
	["comment", "### (1)"]
]

----------------------------------------------------

An escaped \# is a literal in a rule, not the start of a comment.
